---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MainShell from '../components/MainShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Visual Subnet Splitter – CIDR Partitioner | DevSubnet"
  description="Visual Subnet Splitter for CIDR partitioning and network division. Divide IP blocks visually with descriptive labels, merge ranges, and export Terraform-ready HCL configurations for AWS, Azure, and GCP infrastructure planning."
>
  <MainShell activeTab="splitter">
    <div class="related-tools" style="margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Related Tools</h3>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr)); gap: 0.5rem;">
        <a href="/" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">IPv4 Calc</a>
        <a href="/kubernetes-subnet-planner" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">K8s Planner</a>
        <a href="/vlsm-calculator" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">VLSM Calc</a>
        <a href="/subnet-overlap-checker" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">Overlap Checker</a>
        <a href="/cidr-cheat-sheet" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">CIDR Sheet</a>
        <a href="/ipv6-subnet-calculator" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">IPv6 Calc</a>
        <a href="/terraform-subnet-planner" style="color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;">Terraform Planner</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </MainShell>

  <!-- FAQ Schema for SEO -->
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is CIDR supernetting and how does it work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "CIDR supernetting (also called route summarization) combines multiple contiguous networks into a single larger prefix. For example, 192.168.0.0/24 through 192.168.3.0/24 collapse into a single 192.168.0.0/22 summary route, reducing routing table size and improving router performance."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I split a network into smaller subnets?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "To split a network, increase the CIDR prefix length by borrowing host bits. For example, splitting a /24 network into two subnets requires borrowing 1 bit, which increases the prefix to /25 – creating two subnets each containing 128 total IPs (126 usable each)."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the difference between a /16 and /24 subnet?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A /16 subnet allocates 16 bits to the network portion and 16 bits to host addresses, supporting up to 65,534 usable hosts. A /24 subnet allocates 24 bits to the network portion and 8 bits to hosts, supporting up to 254 usable hosts."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many usable hosts are in a /24 subnet?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A /24 subnet has 256 total IP addresses. Subtracting 2 addresses for the network and broadcast leaves exactly 254 usable host IP addresses."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use the Visual Subnet Splitter for Terraform planning?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, the Visual Subnet Splitter allows you to divide network blocks visually and export copy-pasteable IaC configurations for Terraform, AWS, Azure, and GCP without CIDR overlap bugs."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
